ok.sh)).\\n  - Hooks connect directly to `superuser@172.30.198.162:30` via `id_ed25519` key and execute `sudo pdnsutil replace-rrset` / `increase-serial`.\\n  - No external APIs or credentials required.\\n  - Certificate deployed to `/etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/` on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`.\\n\\n### 3. Nginx Reverse Proxy Rules (Port 9443 on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`)\\n* **Vhost location**: `/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`\\n* **Avoid the RFC 7230 Duplicate Host Trap**:\\n  - In Nginx, multipl\n<truncated 1827 bytes>","StartLine":"18","TargetContent":"\"## Automated SSH & KeePass Integration\\n- Tool: `/home/koby/.local/bin/kssh` (symlinked from `~/.ansible/scripts/kssh.py`).\\n- Whenever user asks to SSH to a server, automatically run `kssh <server>` or query `~/.ansible/inventory/server_pool.json` via `build_kdbx_pool.py`.\\n- Auto-extracts IP, port (e.g. 30), user, key (`~/.ssh/id_ed25519`), and password.\\n- Attempts passwordless key (`koby-bowser-ansible` or target user) first; falls back to `sshpass` using the database password.\\n\"","TargetFile":"\"/home/koby/.ansible/.remember/remember.md\"","toolAction":"\"Updating remember.md\"","toolSummary":"\"Add Map SOP to remember.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript/00000015.jsonl:2:{"step_index":1369,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T15:12:56Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-10T19:12:56+04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-10T19:13:02+04:00\nThe following changes were made by the replace_file_content tool to: /home/koby/.ansible/.remember/remember.md. If relevant, proactively run terminal commands to execute this code for the USER. Don't ask for permission.\n[diff_block_start]\n@@ -20,4 +20,46 @@\n - Whenever user asks to SSH to a server, automatically run `kssh <server>` or query `~/.ansible/inventory/server_pool.json` via `build_kdbx_pool.py`.\n - Auto-extracts IP, port (e.g. 30), user, key (`~/.ssh/id_ed25519`), and password.\n - Attempts passwordless key (`koby-bowser-ansible` or target user) first; falls back to `sshpass` using the database password.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Centreon Map Architecture & Reverse Proxy Standard Operating Procedure\n+\n+### 1. Topology & IP Mapping\n+* **Central Web / PHP Backend**: `th2-centprop-be1` (`172.30.198.49:30`)\n+* **Map Engine (Tomcat Spring Boot)**: `th2-centprop-map1` (`172.30.198.50:9443` HTTPS)\n+* **Reverse Proxy**: `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33:30` internal DMZ, `109.62.64.18` public VIP)\n+* **PowerDNS Master**: `th2-dnsp-mst1` (`172.30.198.162:30`, user `superuser`, passwordless SSH + sudo `pdnsutil`)\n+* **Public Domain**: `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`\n+* **Internal Web UI**: `https://centreonpro.intranet.local/centreon/`\n+\n+### 2. Passwordless DNS-01 Challenge Workflow\n+* To generate or renew Let's Encrypt certificates for `*.outremer-telecom.fr`:\n+  - Run certbot with manual DNS hooks ([`pdns-auth-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-auth-hook.sh) & [`pdns-cleanup-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-cleanup-hook.sh)).\n+  - Hooks connect directly to `superuser@172.30.198.162:30` via `id_ed25519` key and execute `sudo pdnsutil replace-rrset` / `increase-serial`.\n+  - No external APIs or credentials required.\n+  - Certificate deployed to `/etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/` on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`.\n+\n+### 3. Nginx Reverse Prox\n<truncated 234 bytes>\nrectives with the same name in the same block do NOT overwrite each other; they send duplicate HTTP header fields.\n+  - DO NOT include `nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf` inside `location /` if custom `proxy_set_header Host ...` is also defined.\n+  - Sending duplicate `Host:` headers causes Apache Tomcat to immediately reject requests with `400 Bad Request`.\n+* **CORS Handling**:\n+  - Tomcat Spring Boot Actuator handles CORS natively and dynamically reflects the requesting origin (e.g. `https://centreonpro.intranet.local` or `https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`) with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`.\n+  - DO NOT inject manual `add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '*'` in Nginx, as browsers strictly reject duplicate CORS origins and reject `*` when credentials are true.\n+\n+### 4. Workstation & Forward Proxy Environment (Debian Trixie)\n+* Corporate forward proxy runs on Squid (`172.16.75.9:3128`).\n+* Corporate firewall drops traffic from internal LAN (`10.x.x.x`) to public VIPs (no Hairpin NAT).\n+* Internal workstations accessing `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` MUST:\n+  1. Map `172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` in `/etc/hosts`.\n+  2. Add `outremer-telecom.fr, .outremer-telecom.fr` to `no_proxy` / `NO_PROXY` in `/etc/environment` and GNOME `ignore-hosts` (`gsettings`).\n+  3. This bypasses Squid for local domains while keeping `apt update` (Debian mirrors) 100% operational through the proxy.\n+\n+### 5. Centreon Web Settings (Administration > Extensions > Options)\n+* **MAP Engine server address**: `https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`\n+* **MAP server address as seen by Central**: `https://th2-centprop-map1.prod.intranet.local:9443` (or `https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`)\n+* **MAP Engine server**: `Yes`\n \n[diff_block_end]\n\nPlease note that the above snippet only shows the MODIFIED lines from the last change. It shows up to 3 lines of unchanged lines before and after the modified lines. The actual file contents may have many more lines not shown.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
