/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript_full/00000009.jsonl:47:{"step_index":634,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T13:24:23Z","thinking":"**Examining DNS Authentication Hook**\n\nThe agent now has passwordless root access and `sudo pdnsutil` execution rights, allowing deeper investigation of the DNS authentication and cleanup hooks. The focus is on the implementation of these scripts to understand their operational logic.\nThe goal is to analyze the scripts located in the specified directory to check the logic, which will be the next step.\n\n\n**Analyzing DNS Record Updates**\n\nThe script first determines the PowerDNS zone and relative name based on the certificate domain, handling several specific domain cases. Then, it utilizes SSH to securely execute commands on the specified PowerDNS host to update the TXT record with the validation string and increments the serial number for the zone.\nIt attempts to verify the propagation of the updated DNS record by querying both Google and Cloudflare DNS resolvers for the updated TXT record.\n\n\n**Verifying DNS Propagation Logic**\n\nThe authentication script now includes a loop that checks for the propagation of the newly created TXT record against two public DNS resolvers, requiring consecutive successful checks before continuing. It uses a local check against the PowerDNS master server as a fallback in case of delays in the public DNS propagation.\nA timeout mechanism is incorporated, exiting with an error if the record doesn't propagate within a specified timeframe.\n\n**Analyzing DNS Cleanup Hook**\n\nThe cleanup hook script determines the DNS zone and corresponding label based on the certificate domain. It similarly handles several specific domain cases, and correctly constructs the relative label for subdomain challenges.\nThe script appears to consistently construct the full DNS record name needed to remove the TXT record, but this will need to be confirmed with other steps.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"ZONE=\"outremer-telecom.fr\"\nCERTBOT_DOMAIN=\"map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\"\nCERTBOT_VALIDATION=\"dry-run-test-token\"\n\nRELATIVE=\"${CERTBOT_DOMAIN%.${ZONE}}\"\nLABEL=\"_acme-challenge.${RELATIVE%.}\"\n\necho \"Zone: $ZONE, Label: $LABEL\"\n\n# Add\nssh -p 30 superuser@172.30.198.162 \"sudo pdnsutil replace-rrset '$ZONE' '$LABEL' TXT 60 '\\\"$CERTBOT_VALIDATION\\\"' && sudo pdnsutil increase-serial '$ZONE'\"\n\n# Check local\ndig +short TXT \"${LABEL}.${ZONE}\" @172.30.198.162\n\n# Clean\nssh -p 30 superuser@172.30.198.162 \"sudo pdnsutil delete-rrset '$ZONE' '$LABEL' TXT && sudo pdnsutil increase-serial '$ZONE'\"","Cwd":"/home/koby","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":8000,"toolAction":"Testing hook command sequence","toolSummary":"Test hook logic on th2-dnsp-mst1"}}]}
