/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript_full/00000017.jsonl:20:{"step_index":1348,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T15:04:30Z","content":"**SKADOOSH! That is what I am talking about!** \n\nBoth checkmarks <span style=\"color:green;font-weight:bold;\">GREEN</span> and the Map interface fully loaded and rendering cleanly! \n\n---\n\n### Quick Recap of What We Conquered:\n\n1. **Passwordless DNS-01 Let's Encrypt Issuance**: Automated DNS challenge injection directly into PowerDNS Master (`th2-dnsp-mst1`) via `id_ed25519` key without APIs or passwords.\n2. **Dedicated Nginx Vhost (`03-map...`)**: Decoupled port `9443` into a dedicated, clean configuration listening on both internal DMZ and public VIP with its own independent access/error logs.\n3. **Tomcat RFC 7230 Compliance**: Eradicated the duplicate `Host:` header that was triggering Tomcat's strict `400 Bad Request`.\n4. **Clean Native CORS Handshake**: Eliminated double-origin header conflicts so Firefox and Chromium accept the actuator telemetry and map streams natively with credentials.\n5. **Internal Proxy Bypass**: Configured workstation `no_proxy` and GNOME exceptions so office workstations talk directly to the reverse proxy while leaving your Squid proxy and `apt update` 100% operational.\n\nDon't forget to click **Save** at the bottom of the **Administration > Extensions > Options** page so Centreon persists those URLs in the database!\n\nEverything is documented and archived in your report artifact:  \n[centreon-map-chain-report.md](file:///home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/centreon-map-chain-report.md).\n\nEnjoy your fully operational Centreon Map!","thinking":"**Celebrating Successful Infrastructure Deployment**\n\nExcellent! The user confirms a green test result and proper map UI loading. The Let's Encrypt production issuance is now verified. Another victory for flawless execution!\n\n\n"}
/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript_full/00000017.jsonl:22:{"step_index":1350,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T15:07:05Z","content":"Voici un paragraphe clair et professionnel prêt à être envoyé au NOC :\n\n---\n\n> **Objet :** Résolution de la connectivité et intégration de Centreon Map (port 9443)\n>\n> Bonjour l'équipe,\n> \n> L'incident d'accès au moteur Centreon Map (`https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`) est désormais entièrement résolu. Le problème provenait de deux causes sur le reverse proxy Nginx (`th2-revproxyp-fe1`) : d'une part, un rejet **HTTP 400 Bad Request** de Tomcat causé par l'envoi d'en-têtes `Host` dupliqués (violation stricte de la RFC 7230), et d'autre part, un blocage de sécurité **CORS** par les navigateurs web dû à un conflit d'en-têtes d'origine sur les requêtes cross-ports (443 vers 9443). Pour corriger la situation, nous avons déployé un vhost Nginx dédié adossé à un certificat SSL Let's Encrypt officiel valide (généré via challenge DNS-01 sur `th2-dnsp-mst1`), assaini les directives de proxification pour supprimer les doublons d'en-têtes HTTP, et laissé Tomcat restituer nativement ses en-têtes CORS dynamiques avec support des credentials. Tous les tests de connexion Centreon sont passés au vert et la cartographie est de nouveau parfaitement opérationnelle.","thinking":"**Drafting the French Email**\n\nL'intégration de Centreon Map rencontrait des problèmes. Après investigation, la configuration des ports de communication entre les services était incorrecte, causant des erreurs de connexion. La correction a consisté à ajuster les ports de communication dans la configuration pour correspondre aux spécifications attendues, rétablissant ainsi la communication et le bon fonctionnement de l'intégration.\n\n\n"}
/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript_full/00000017.jsonl:30:{"step_index":1358,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T15:11:11Z","thinking":"**Documenting Configuration Details**\n\nInitial focus is on documenting the Centreon Map reverse proxy architecture and passwordless DNS-01 Let's Encrypt issuance through PowerDNS, specifically `th2-dnsp-mst1`. Next, documenting a Tomcat RFC 7230 duplicate `Host:` trap and a dual CORS conflict trap is needed. Finally, consider documenting internal network routing and proxy bypass for `outremer-telecom.fr`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Append Centreon Map & Reverse Proxy Architecture rules and memory","EndLine":61,"Instruction":"Add Section on Centreon Map & Reverse Proxy Architecture","ReplacementContent":"* Verify status reports `ONLINE` with accurate OS and kernel details.\n\n---\n\n## Centreon Map Architecture & Reverse Proxy Standard Operating Procedure\n\n### 1. Topology & IP Mapping\n* **Central Web / PHP Backend**: `th2-centprop-be1` (`172.30.198.49:30`)\n* **Map Engine (Tomcat Spring Boot)**: `th2-centprop-map1` (`172.30.198.50:9443` HTTPS)\n* **Reverse Proxy**: `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33:30` internal DMZ, `109.62.64.18` public VIP)\n* **PowerDNS Master**: `th2-dnsp-mst1` (`172.30.198.162:30`, user `superuser`, passwordless SSH + sudo `pdnsutil`)\n* **Public Domain**: `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`\n\n### 2. Passwordless DNS-01 Challenge Workflow\n* To generate or renew Let's Encrypt certificates for `*.outremer-telecom.fr`:\n  - Run certbot with manual DNS hooks ([`pdns-auth-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-auth-hook.sh) & [`pdns-cleanup-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-cleanup-hook.sh)).\n  - Hooks connect directly to `superuser@172.30.198.162:30` via `id_ed25519` key and execute `sudo pdnsutil replace-rrset` / `increase-serial`.\n  - No external APIs or credentials required.\n\n### 3. Nginx Reverse Proxy Rules (Port 9443 on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`)\n* **Vhost location**: `/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`\n* **Avoid the RFC 7230 Duplicate Host Trap**:\n  - In Nginx, multiple `proxy_set_header` directives with the same name in the same block do NOT overwrite each other; they send duplicate HTTP header fields.\n  - DO NOT include `nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf` inside `location /` if custom `proxy_set_header Host ...` is also defined.\n  - Sending duplicate `Host:` headers causes Apache Tomcat to immediately reject requests with `400 Bad Request`.\n* **CORS Handling**:\n  - Tomcat Spring Boot Actuator handles CORS natively and dynamically reflects the requesting origin (e.g. `https://centreonpro.intranet.local` or `https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`) with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`.\n  - DO NOT inject manual `add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '*'` in Nginx, as browsers strictly reject duplicate CORS origins and reject `*` when credentials are true.\n\n### 4. Workstation & Forward Proxy Environment (Debian Trixie)\n* Corporate forward proxy runs on Squid (`172.16.75.9:3128`).\n* Corporate firewall drops traffic from internal LAN (`10.x.x.x`) to public VIPs (no Hairpin NAT).\n* Internal workstations accessing `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` MUST:\n  1. Map `172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` in `/etc/hosts`.\n  2. Add `outremer-telecom.fr, .outremer-telecom.fr` to `no_proxy` / `NO_PROXY` in `/etc/environment` and GNOME `ignore-hosts` (`gsettings`).\n  3. This bypasses Squid for local domains while keeping `apt update` (Debian mirrors) 100% operational through the proxy.\n","StartLine":60,"TargetContent":"* Verify status reports `ONLINE` with accurate OS and kernel details.\n","TargetFile":"/home/koby/.gemini/config/AGENTS.md","toolAction":"Committing knowledge to AGENTS.md","toolSummary":"Update AGENTS.md memory"}}]}
/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript_full/00000017.jsonl:39:{"step_index":1368,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T15:12:49Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Add Centreon Map & Reverse Proxy memory to remember.md","EndLine":23,"Instruction":"Append Centreon Map & Reverse Proxy memory and status","ReplacementContent":"## Automated SSH & KeePass Integration\n- Tool: `/home/koby/.local/bin/kssh` (symlinked from `~/.ansible/scripts/kssh.py`).\n- Whenever user asks to SSH to a server, automatically run `kssh <server>` or query `~/.ansible/inventory/server_pool.json` via `build_kdbx_pool.py`.\n- Auto-extracts IP, port (e.g. 30), user, key (`~/.ssh/id_ed25519`), and password.\n- Attempts passwordless key (`koby-bowser-ansible` or target user) first; falls back to `sshpass` using the database password.\n\n---\n\n## Centreon Map Architecture & Reverse Proxy Standard Operating Procedure\n\n### 1. Topology & IP Mapping\n* **Central Web / PHP Backend**: `th2-centprop-be1` (`172.30.198.49:30`)\n* **Map Engine (Tomcat Spring Boot)**: `th2-centprop-map1` (`172.30.198.50:9443` HTTPS)\n* **Reverse Proxy**: `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33:30` internal DMZ, `109.62.64.18` public VIP)\n* **PowerDNS Master**: `th2-dnsp-mst1` (`172.30.198.162:30`, user `superuser`, passwordless SSH + sudo `pdnsutil`)\n* **Public Domain**: `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`\n* **Internal Web UI**: `https://centreonpro.intranet.local/centreon/`\n\n### 2. Passwordless DNS-01 Challenge Workflow\n* To generate or renew Let's Encrypt certificates for `*.outremer-telecom.fr`:\n  - Run certbot with manual DNS hooks ([`pdns-auth-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-auth-hook.sh) & [`pdns-cleanup-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-cleanup-hook.sh)).\n  - Hooks connect directly to `superuser@172.30.198.162:30` via `id_ed25519` key and execute `sudo pdnsutil replace-rrset` / `increase-serial`.\n  - No external APIs or credentials required.\n  - Certificate deployed to `/etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/` on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`.\n\n### 3. Nginx Reverse Proxy Rules (Port 9443 on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`)\n* **Vhost location**: `/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`\n* **Avoid the RFC 7230 Duplicate Host Trap**:\n  - In Nginx, multiple `proxy_set_header` directives with the same name in the same block do NOT overwrite each other; they send duplicate HTTP header fields.\n  - DO NOT include `nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf` inside `location /` if custom `proxy_set_header Host ...` is also defined.\n  - Sending duplicate `Host:` headers causes Apache Tomcat to immediately reject requests with `400 Bad Request`.\n* **CORS Handling**:\n  - Tomcat Spring Boot Actuator handles CORS natively and dynamically reflects the requesting origin (e.g. `https://centreonpro.intranet.local` or `https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`) with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`.\n  - DO NOT inject manual `add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '*'` in Nginx, as browsers strictly reject duplicate CORS origins and reject `*` when credentials are true.\n\n### 4. Workstation & Forward Proxy Environment (Debian Trixie)\n* Corporate forward proxy runs on Squid (`172.16.75.9:3128`).\n* Corporate firewall drops traffic from internal LAN (`10.x.x.x`) to public VIPs (no Hairpin NAT).\n* Internal workstations accessing `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` MUST:\n  1. Map `172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` in `/etc/hosts`.\n  2. Add `outremer-telecom.fr, .outremer-telecom.fr` to `no_proxy` / `NO_PROXY` in `/etc/environment` and GNOME `ignore-hosts` (`gsettings`).\n  3. This bypasses Squid for local domains while keeping `apt update` (Debian mirrors) 100% operational through the proxy.\n\n### 5. Centreon Web Settings (Administration > Extensions > Options)\n* **MAP Engine server address**: `https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`\n* **MAP server address as seen by Central**: `https://th2-centprop-map1.prod.intranet.local:9443` (or `https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`)\n* **MAP Engine server**: `Yes`\n","StartLine":18,"TargetContent":"## Automated SSH & KeePass Integration\n- Tool: `/home/koby/.local/bin/kssh` (symlinked from `~/.ansible/scripts/kssh.py`).\n- Whenever user asks to SSH to a server, automatically run `kssh <server>` or query `~/.ansible/inventory/server_pool.json` via `build_kdbx_pool.py`.\n- Auto-extracts IP, port (e.g. 30), user, key (`~/.ssh/id_ed25519`), and password.\n- Attempts passwordless key (`koby-bowser-ansible` or target user) first; falls back to `sshpass` using the database password.\n","TargetFile":"/home/koby/.ansible/.remember/remember.md","toolAction":"Updating remember.md","toolSummary":"Add Map SOP to remember.md"}}]}
/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript_full/00000017.jsonl:40:{"step_index":1369,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T15:12:56Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-10T19:12:56+04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-10T19:13:02+04:00\nThe following changes were made by the replace_file_content tool to: /home/koby/.ansible/.remember/remember.md. If relevant, proactively run terminal commands to execute this code for the USER. Don't ask for permission.\n[diff_block_start]\n@@ -20,4 +20,46 @@\n - Whenever user asks to SSH to a server, automatically run `kssh <server>` or query `~/.ansible/inventory/server_pool.json` via `build_kdbx_pool.py`.\n - Auto-extracts IP, port (e.g. 30), user, key (`~/.ssh/id_ed25519`), and password.\n - Attempts passwordless key (`koby-bowser-ansible` or target user) first; falls back to `sshpass` using the database password.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Centreon Map Architecture & Reverse Proxy Standard Operating Procedure\n+\n+### 1. Topology & IP Mapping\n+* **Central Web / PHP Backend**: `th2-centprop-be1` (`172.30.198.49:30`)\n+* **Map Engine (Tomcat Spring Boot)**: `th2-centprop-map1` (`172.30.198.50:9443` HTTPS)\n+* **Reverse Proxy**: `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33:30` internal DMZ, `109.62.64.18` public VIP)\n+* **PowerDNS Master**: `th2-dnsp-mst1` (`172.30.198.162:30`, user `superuser`, passwordless SSH + sudo `pdnsutil`)\n+* **Public Domain**: `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`\n+* **Internal Web UI**: `https://centreonpro.intranet.local/centreon/`\n+\n+### 2. Passwordless DNS-01 Challenge Workflow\n+* To generate or renew Let's Encrypt certificates for `*.outremer-telecom.fr`:\n+  - Run certbot with manual DNS hooks ([`pdns-auth-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-auth-hook.sh) & [`pdns-cleanup-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-cleanup-hook.sh)).\n+  - Hooks connect directly to `superuser@172.30.198.162:30` via `id_ed25519` key and execute `sudo pdnsutil replace-rrset` / `increase-serial`.\n+  - No external APIs or credentials required.\n+  - Certificate deployed to `/etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/` on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`.\n+\n+### 3. Nginx Reverse Proxy Rules (Port 9443 on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`)\n+* **Vhost location**: `/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`\n+* **Avoid the RFC 7230 Duplicate Host Trap**:\n+  - In Nginx, multiple `proxy_set_header` directives with the same name in the same block do NOT overwrite each other; they send duplicate HTTP header fields.\n+  - DO NOT include `nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf` inside `location /` if custom `proxy_set_header Host ...` is also defined.\n+  - Sending duplicate `Host:` headers causes Apache Tomcat to immediately reject requests with `400 Bad Request`.\n+* **CORS Handling**:\n+  - Tomcat Spring Boot Actuator handles CORS natively and dynamically reflects the requesting origin (e.g. `https://centreonpro.intranet.local` or `https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`) with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`.\n+  - DO NOT inject manual `add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '*'` in Nginx, as browsers strictly reject duplicate CORS origins and reject `*` when credentials are true.\n+\n+### 4. Workstation & Forward Proxy Environment (Debian Trixie)\n+* Corporate forward proxy runs on Squid (`172.16.75.9:3128`).\n+* Corporate firewall drops traffic from internal LAN (`10.x.x.x`) to public VIPs (no Hairpin NAT).\n+* Internal workstations accessing `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` MUST:\n+  1. Map `172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` in `/etc/hosts`.\n+  2. Add `outremer-telecom.fr, .outremer-telecom.fr` to `no_proxy` / `NO_PROXY` in `/etc/environment` and GNOME `ignore-hosts` (`gsettings`).\n+  3. This bypasses Squid for local domains while keeping `apt update` (Debian mirrors) 100% operational through the proxy.\n+\n+### 5. Centreon Web Settings (Administration > Extensions > Options)\n+* **MAP Engine server address**: `https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`\n+* **MAP server address as seen by Central**: `https://th2-centprop-map1.prod.intranet.local:9443` (or `https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`)\n+* **MAP Engine server**: `Yes`\n \n[diff_block_end]\n\nPlease note that the above snippet only shows the MODIFIED lines from the last change. It shows up to 3 lines of unchanged lines before and after the modified lines. The actual file contents may have many more lines not shown."}
