ranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/` **without `-k`**.\n   * Returned `HTTP/2 301` redirecting to `/centreon-map/` with **zero SSL certificate warnings**.\n\n---\n\n### Next Action\n\nYou can now click **\"Test connection to server\"** in Centreon Web (`Administration > Extensions > Options`). The test will validate with a green success mark."}
/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/tasks/task-956.log:609:/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/tasks/task-956.log:122:/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl:900:{"step_index":903,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:11:27Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. In the .ansible folder, there is playbook to issue cert. Can you check?\n2. Can you run the playbook?\n3. For the DNS challenge, ypu must use the th2-dnsp-mst1\n4. For option 1 what you will need?\n5. To connect to th2-dnsp-mst1, it is passwordless! No API is required!\n6. I am still getting failed connection! Please list the flow but do not connect please\n7. Can you capture via tcpdump on the reverse proxy when I do a connection from the backend?\n8. I used the IP but now I will test with FQDN.\n9. Launched!\n10. How to fix this?\n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n* **Objective**: Configure and validate the reverse proxy chain for Centreon Map (`172.30.198.50:9443`) via `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33:9443`) and Centreon Central Web (`th2-centprop-be1` — `172.30.198.49:443`), so the **\"Test connection to server\"** button for `MAP Engine server address` succeeds.\n* **Core Discovery**: The \"Test connection to server\" button for `MAP Engine server address` is **NOT executed by PHP on the Central backend**, but is executed **client-side directly in the user's web browser** via JavaScript AJAX ([`listOptions.js:266`](file:///usr/share/centreon/www/modules/centreon-map4-web-client/views/options/listOptions.js#L266)).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n* **DNS-01 Certificate Issued**:\n  * Issued official Let's Encrypt production certificate for `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` (valid until Dec 9, 2026).\n  * Method: Executed from local Debian Trixie workstation using Certbot manual hooks with **passwordless SSH** (`id_ed25519`) to `superuser@172.30.198.162:30` (`th2-dnsp-mst1`) and `sudo pdnsutil replace-rrset` / `increase-serial`.\n  * Verified public propagation against Google DoH and Cloudflare DoH.\n* **Certificate & Vhost Deployed on `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33`)**:\n  * Certificate files deployed to `/etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/`.\n  * Created dedicated, independent vhost [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) listening explicitly on `172.30.198.33:9443` and `109.62.64.18:9443`.\n  * Removed port 9443 block from `02-extranetclient...conf`.\n  * `nginx -t` verified OK and Nginx reloaded cleanly.\n  * Verified with `openssl s_client`: `CN=map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`, Issuer `Let's Encrypt (YE2)`.\n* **Central Backend Resolution**:\n  * Verified that `th2-centprop-be1` (`172.30.198.49`) curls `https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/` **without `-k`** and TLS validation passes cleanly (`HTTP/2 301` to `/centreon-map/`).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Root Cause of Current Failure\n1. **The Code Behind the Test Button**:\n   In `/usr/share/centreon/www/modules/centreon-map4-web-client/views/options/listOptions.js`:\n   * `testInternalServerAddressNg()` calls `${baseUrl}/centreon/api/latest/map/check-health` (PHP server-side cURL), which is why that button succeeded.\n   * `testServerAddressNg()` runs `jQuery.ajax({ type: 'GET', url: `${urlServerNg}/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health` })` **directly from the user's browser**.\n2. **Workstation Hairpin NAT Block**:\n   * Internal PCs (e.g. testing workstation) resolve `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` $\\rightarrow$ `109.62.64.18`.\n   * Testing confirmed: `nc -zv 109.62.64.18 9443` times out because the corporate firewall drops internal traffic to its public VIP (no Hairpin NAT).\n   * In contrast, `nc -zv 172.30.198.33 9443` succeeds instantly.\n3. **CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing) Missing on Port 9443**:\n   * Browser is on `https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` (port 443).\n   * AJAX target is `https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443` (port 9443).\n   * Different port = different Origin. Browsers block the AJAX call unless Nginx returns `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`.\n4. **Tomcat 400 Bad Request on Nginx Proxy**:\n   * Direct to Tomcat from `.49`: `curl -k -H 'Host: map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443' https://172.30.198.50:9443/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health` returns `200 {\"status\":\"UP\"}`.\n   * Through Nginx reverse proxy: returns `HTTP Status 400 – Bad Request`.\n   * Root cause: `include nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf;` in Nginx sends RFC 7239 `Forwarded: $proxy_add_forwarded;` which Tomcat / Spring Boot Actuator rejects as malformed.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Active Context\n* **Reverse Proxy**: `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33:30`), managed via `/home/koby/.ansible/kssh`.\n* **Backend**: `th2-centprop-be1` (`172.30.198.49:30`), managed via `/home/koby/.ansible/kssh`.\n* **DNS Master**: `th2-dnsp-mst1` (`172.30.198.162:30`), passwordless SSH with `superuser` and `sudo pdnsutil`.\n* **Nginx Configuration**: `/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf` on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Next Steps to Fix the Connection\n1. **Fix `03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf` on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`**:\n   * Remove `include nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf;` (or unset `proxy_set_header Forwarded;`).\n   * Add CORS headers:\n     ```nginx\n     add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '$http_origin' always;\n     add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Methods' 'GET, POST, OPTIONS' always;\n     add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Headers' 'DNT,User-Agent,X-Requested-With,If-Modified-Since,Cache-Control,Content-Type,Range,Authorization' always;\n     add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Credentials' 'true' always;\n     if ($request_method = 'OPTIONS') {\n         return 204;\n     }\n     ```\n   * Set standard proxy headers: `Host $http_host;`, `X-Real-IP $remote_addr;`, `X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;`, `X-Forwarded-Proto https;`.\n   * Verify `curl -sS https://map...:9443/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health` through Nginx returns `200 {\"status\":\"UP\"}`.\n2. **Workstation DNS Resolution (for Internal Testing)**:\n   * To test from an internal workstation, add `172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` to the local workstation's `/etc/hosts` (or configure corporate split-horizon DNS) to bypass the lack of Hairpin NAT on the firewall.\n3. **Verify in Centreon Web UI**:\n   * Click **\"Test connection to server\"**; browser AJAX will receive `200 {\"status\":\"UP\"}` with matching CORS headers and turn green.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n* Do not restart Nginx (always `systemctl reload nginx` after `nginx -t`).\n* Never modify shared configurations without strict scoping.\n* Respect user instructions on network testing and commands.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 2 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.agents/agents/koby-bowser-nginx/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-10T07:28:04Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: centreon-map-chain-report]\nPath: file:///home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/centreon-map-chain-report.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-10T13:39:29Z\n\n# Running Background Tasks\nThe following background tasks were running at the time this checkpoint was 