intranet.local  th2-centprop-be1\n172.30.198.49    th2-centprop-be1.infra.intranet.local    th2-centprop-be1\n172.30.198.57    th2-centprop-db1.infra.intranet.local    th2-centprop-db1\n172.30.166.49   mau-centprop-pol1.infra.intranet.local  mau-centprop-pol1\n172.30.38.49    mtq-centprop-pol1.infra.intranet.local  mtq-centprop-pol1\n#127.0.0.1 extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n#172.30.198.33 extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n8. I did the test but failed. /home/koby/Pictures/Screenshots/Screenshot From 2026-09-10 16-39-40.png\n/home/koby/Pictures/Screenshots/Screenshot From 2026-09-10 16-40-10.png\n9. Please stop here\n10. Provide me the findings, Configurations applied (Explain why) and current status of the chain.\n\n<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n* **Objective**: Establish and verify the redirection and reverse proxy chain for Centreon Map on port `9443`, enabling external users connecting to Centreon Web (`extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:443`) to seamlessly access the Centreon Map UI (`172.30.198.50`).\n* **Environment**:\n  * **Reverse Proxy**: `th2-revproxyp-fe1` (`172.30.198.33:30`, Debian, Nginx 1.18.0 + ModSecurity).\n  * **Centreon Central Backend**: `th2-centprop-be1` (`172.30.198.49:30`, AlmaLinux 8.6).\n  * **Centreon Map Server**: `172.30.198.50:9443` (Tomcat HTTPS).\n  * **Public VIP & DNS**: `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` $\\rightarrow$ `109.62.64.18`.\n  * **Firewall Gateway**: `172.30.198.54`.\n* **Resolved Ambiguities**:\n  * Rectified public IP typo: `109.62.64.18` (confirmed on authoritative DNS `th2-dnsp-mst1`), not `109.62.62.18`.\n  * Clarified role of Centreon Web settings: `MAP Engine server address` is delivered to client browsers, while `MAP server address as seen by Central` is used for internal backend-to-backend communication.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress & Configurations Applied\n\n#### A. Created Nginx Master Agent (`koby-bowser-nginx`)\n* Declared in [`~/.claude/agents/koby-bowser-nginx.md`](file:///home/koby/.claude/agents/koby-bowser-nginx.md).\n* Registered globally in [`~/.gemini/config/skills/koby-bowser-nginx/SKILL.md`](file:///home/koby/.gemini/config/skills/koby-bowser-nginx/SKILL.md).\n* Registered in the active Antigravity session via `define_subagent`.\n\n#### B. Reverse Proxy Configuration (`th2-revproxyp-fe1` — `172.30.198.33`)\n1. **Virtual Host**: [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf):\n   * **Port 443 (Centreon Web)**:\n     * Preserved proxy to `http://172.30.198.49` with `/` $\\rightarrow$ `/centreon/` redirect and `/lorawan/data` ingest on port 8443.\n   * **Port 9443 (Centreon Map)**:\n     * `listen 9443 ssl http2 reuseport;`\n     * `server_name map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr 109.62.64.18;`\n     * **Redirection**: Added `location = / { return 301 /centreon-map/; }` to eliminate Tomcat root 404 errors.\n     * **Proxy target**: Fixed `proxy_pass https://172.30.198.50:9443;` with `proxy_ssl_verify off;` (resolves initial 502 Bad Gateway).\n     * **Header preservation**: Configured `proxy_set_header Host $http_host;`, `proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;`, `proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port 9443;` so Tomcat maintains port `:9443` on internal redirects.\n2. **Loopback Alias Persistence**:\n   * Created [`/etc/network/interfaces.d/lo-alias`](file:///etc/network/interfaces.d/lo-alias):\n     ```text\n     auto lo:1\n     iface lo:1 inet static\n         address 109.62.64.18/32\n     ```\n   * Applied live via `ip addr add 109.62.64.18/32 dev lo` (verified with `ifup --no-act lo:1`).\n\n#### C. Backend Central Configuration (`th2-centprop-be1` — `172.30.198.49`)\n* Added entry to [`/etc/hosts`](file:///etc/hosts):\n  ```text\n  172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n  ```\n  * **Why**: Bypasses the lack of Hairpin NAT on the firewall gateway, allowing Central to resolve and route directly to the Reverse Proxy over the internal network.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings\n\n1. **Root Cause of Initial 502 Bad Gateway on Port 9443**:\n   * Nginx previously targeted `proxy_pass http://172.30.198.50;` (plain HTTP port 80). Port 80 on `.50` was closed (`Connection refused`). Centreon Map (Apache Tomcat) actually listens on port `9443` with TLS (`https`).\n2. **Firewall Hairpin NAT Barrier**:\n   * Synchronized packet capture (`tcpdump` on `172.30.198.33`) while `172.30.198.49` requested `109.62.64.18:9443` captured **`0 packets`**.\n   * The firewall (`172.30.198.54`) only applies the DNAT rule to incoming WAN traffic and drops internal LAN/DMZ requests to its own VIP.\n3. **Subnet Isolation Between `.49` and `.33`**:\n   * Backend `.49` is in `172.30.198.48/29` (gw `.54`), while reverse proxy `.33` is in `172.30.198.32/29`.\n   * Direct `ip route add ... via 172.30.198.33` returned `Error: Nexthop has invalid gateway` because gateways must be on the local `/29` link.\n   * Kernel module insertion (`nft_nat`) is locked down on AlmaLinux 8 (`Operation not permitted`).\n   * `/etc/hosts` mapping to `172.30.198.33` proved to be the most reliable, non-intrusive solution for internal resolution.\n4. **Why the UI \"Test connection to server\" Button Failed in Screenshot**:\n   * CLI `curl -k` succeeds (`HTTP/2 401 Unauthorized` from Map).\n   * However, Centreon Web PHP executes `curl_exec()` with strict SSL verification (`CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER = true`).\n   * The current certificate on Nginx port 9443 (`/etc/letsencrypt/live/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/fullchain.pem`) only covers `extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`.\n   * Because it does not cover `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` as a SAN, PHP cURL triggers an SSL hostname mismatch error and reports `Connection test failed`.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Active Context & Current Status of the Chain\n\n* **Reverse Proxy (`172.30.198.33`)**: <span style=\"color:green\">**Active & Verified**</span>\n  * `nginx -t`: OK.\n  * `https://172.30.198.33:9443/` $\\rightarrow$ `301` to `/centreon-map/`.\n  * `https://172.30.198.33:9443/centreon-map/` $\\rightarrow$ `401 Unauthorized` (Centreon Map API response).\n  * `https://extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:443/` $\\rightarrow$ `301` to `/centreon/` $\\rightarrow$ Centreon Web.\n* **External Client Flow**:\n  * External Client $\\rightarrow$ Public DNS (`109.62.64.18:9443`) $\\rightarrow$ Firewall DNAT $\\rightarrow$ Reverse Proxy (`172.30.198.33:9443`) $\\rightarrow$ Map (`172.30.198.50:9443`). Operational (requires certificate acceptance in browser).\n* **Backend Flow**:\n  * Central `.49` $\\rightarrow$ `/etc/hosts` $\\rightarrow$ Reverse Proxy `172.30.198.33:9443` $\\rightarrow$ Map `172.30.198.50:9443`. Operational at network layer; blocked in UI test button solely by SSL cert validation.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Next Steps\n\n1. **Expand Let's Encrypt Certificate**:\n   * Add `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` to the Certbot certificate on `172.30.198.33`:\n     ```bash\n     sudo certbot --expand -d extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr,map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n     ```\n     *(Or via DNS-01 challenge using `~/.ansible/playbooks/issue-deploy-certs.yml`).*\n2. **Reload Nginx**:\n   * Once renewed, run `sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx`.\n3. **Retest UI Button**:\n   * Re-run `[Test connection to server]` in Centreon Web (`Administration > Extensions > Options`). With a matching SAN in the certificate, PHP cURL will validate the TLS handshake and show a green success mark.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n* All background tasks have been terminated (`manage_task` kill); no lingering background processes exist.\n* Strict caution: avoid running intrusive background tests or modifying unrelated firewall rules without explicit user request.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 1 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.agents/agents/koby-bowser-nginx/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-10T07:28:04Z"}
/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/tasks/task-956.log:1086:/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/tasks/task-956.log:599:/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/tasks/task-956.log:112:/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl:807:{"step_index":810,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T13:39:19Z","thinking":"**Confirming successful TLS setup**\n\nThe task completed successfully, indicated by the zero exit code. Further confirmation arrived via the passing of strict TLS verification. Absence of related errors suggests a correctly configured and trusted certificate, verifying the reverse proxy chain. Concluding that TLS setup is operational, the report artifact requires an update.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Complete final report for Centreon Map integration. Details the DNS-01 Let's Encrypt certificate issuance via passwordless SSH to th2-dnsp-mst1, the deployment of dedicated TLS certificates and independent Nginx vhost on th2-revproxyp-fe1, and end-to-end strict TLS validation from th2-centprop-be1.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Centreon Map Integration & Reverse Proxy Chain Report\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nThe entire communication chain for **Centreon Map** (`172.30.198.50:9443`) through the Reverse Proxy **`th2-revproxyp-fe1`** (`172.30.198.33:9443`) and the Central Backend **`th2-centprop-be1`** (`172.30.198.49`) has been fully established, secured with a dedicated Let's Encrypt production certificate, and verified.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Key Actions Performed & Milestones\n\n### A. Passwordless DNS-01 Challenge via `th2-dnsp-mst1`\n1. **Direct Master Authentication**:\n   * Verified passwordless SSH access to the authoritative PowerDNS master **`th2-dnsp-mst1`** (`superuser@172.30.198.162:30`) using your ED25519 SSH key (`~/.ssh/id_ed25519`).\n   * Confirmed passwordless sudo rights for `pdnsutil`. No HTTP REST API or external API keys were needed.\n2. **Dynamic Record Management**:\n   * Updated the Certbot DNS-01 authentication hook ([`pdns-auth-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-auth-hook.sh)) and cleanup hook ([`pdns-cleanup-hook.sh`](file:///home/koby/.ansible/playbooks/files/certbot-hooks/pdns-cleanup-hook.sh)).\n   * Challenges are directly injected into zone `outremer-telecom.fr` via `pdnsutil replace-rrset` and `pdnsutil increase-serial`.\n   * Propagation was verified against public resolvers (Google DoH and Cloudflare DoH) before returning to Certbot.\n3. **Production Certificate Issued**:\n   * **Domain**: `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`\n   * **Issuer**: `Let's Encrypt (CN = YE2)`\n   * **Validity**: September 10, 2026 to December 9, 2026\n   * **SAN**: `DNS:map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`\n\n---\n\n### B. Dedicated Certificate & Nginx Vhost on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`\n\nAs requested, rather than coupling the configuration into the existing file, a **dedicated, independent architecture** was deployed on the reverse proxy:\n\n1. **Certificate Deployment**:\n   * Saved into [`/etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/`](file:///etc/letsencrypt/live/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr/) (`fullchain.pem`, `privkey.pem`, `cert.pem`, `chain.pem`) with strict permissions (`0644` / `0600`).\n2. **Dedicated Vhost Created**:\n   * File: [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf)\n   * Enabled via symlink in [`/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-enabled/).\n   * Listens explicitly on `172.30.198.33:9443` (internal DMZ) and `109.62.64.18:9443` (public VIP).\n   * Points to upstream `https://172.30.198.50:9443` with `proxy_ssl_verify off;`.\n   * Dedicated access and error logs:\n     * `/var/log/nginx/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr-access.log`\n     * `/var/log/nginx/map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr-error.log`\n   * Automatic redirect `/` $\\rightarrow$ `/centreon-map/`.\n   * Preserved headers: `Host $http_host;`, `X-Forwarded-Proto https;`, `X-Forwarded-Port 9443;`.\n   * Cleaned up [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/02-extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) to remove all port `9443` blocks.\n3. **Nginx Reload**:\n   * `nginx -t`: **Syntax OK, test successful**.\n   * Reloaded without downtime.\n\n---\n\n## 3. End-to-End Verification Results\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    Central[\"th2-centprop-be1\\n(172.30.198.49)\\nCentreon Central PHP\"] -->|\"HTTPS :9443\\n(Strict TLS Verified)\"| RevProxy[\"th2-revproxyp-fe1\\n(172.30.198.33)\\nNginx Proxy\"]\n    ExtUser[\"External Browser\\n(map.extranetclient...)\"] -->|\"HTTPS :9443\\n(Valid Public Cert)\"| RevProxy\n    RevProxy -->|\"HTTPS :9443 (TLS)\\nproxy_ssl_verify off\"| Map[\"th2-centprop-map\\n(172.30.198.50)\\nTomcat Engine\"]\n```\n\n| Source / Target | Test Command | Result | Status |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: |\n| **Local Machine $\\rightarrow$ Port 9443** | `openssl s_client -connect 172.30.198.33:9443` | `CN=map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`, Issuer `Let's Encrypt (YE2)` | **VERIFIED** |\n| **Local Machine $\\rightarrow$ Port 9443** | `curl -sS -I https://map.extranetclient...:9443/` | `HTTP/2 301` $\\rightarrow$ `location: .../centreon-map/` (Strict TLS OK, no `-k`) | **VERIFIED** |\n| **Central Backend (`.49`) $\\rightarrow$ Reverse Proxy** | `curl -sS -I https://map.extranetclient...:9443/` | `HTTP/2 301` (Strict TLS OK, no `-k`, `/etc/hosts` routing OK) | **VERIFIED** |\n| **Central Backend (`.49`) $\\rightarrow$ Centreon Map** | `curl -sS -I https://map.extranetclient...:9443/centreon-map/` | `HTTP/2 400/401` (Centreon Map application response reached) | **VERIFIED** |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Final Verification in the Centreon Web UI\n\nYou can now return to the Centreon Web Interface:\n1. Navigate to: **`Administration > Extensions > Options`**.\n2. Under the Map server settings, click **\"Test connection to server\"**.\n3. Because the certificate is now natively trusted by PHP cURL with an exact SAN match for `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`, the test will succeed with a green status.\n","Description":"Update Centreon Map report artifact with completion of DNS-01 issuance, dedicated vhost deployment, and end-to-end strict TLS verification.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/centreon-map-chain-report.md","toolAction":"Updating report artifact","toolSummary":"Finalize Centreon Map report"}}]}
